id: pm-9gcx61
title: Preserve bounded transport refusal details in dependency advisory collection receipts
description: "The advisory collector correctly refused unavailable registry and OSV evidence, but replaced both underlying errors with status unavailable and a timestamp. Diagnosing this required invoking private feed adapters to discover empty registry output and UND_ERR_CONNECT_TIMEOUT. The same exact queries pass with temporary IPv4-first execution and network family auto-selection disabled. Preserve safe reason codes and bounded transport classification without recording response bodies, credentials or weakening completeness."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 2
tags[3]: agent-ux,diagnostics,security
created_at: "2026-11-09T08:31:50.013Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T08:48:42.162Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 90
acceptance_criteria: Unavailable feeds expose bounded safe reason codes and transport categories for actionable recovery; Raw request and response data and credentials are never persisted; Positive and negative controls preserve all-version independent feed coverage and fail-closed decisions
parent: pm-u9d0
risk: low
confidence: high
expected_result: An unavailable advisory source produces safe actionable transport reasons while independent coverage and fail-closed security decisions remain intact.
